Adopt SDL's KMSDRM EGL context on rk3566 (Path B) - v6, SDL_GL_SwapWindow

Fifth iteration got the context migrated and rendered 4 frames, then
nothing - because GFX_Flip's raw eglSwapBuffers doesn't drive KMSDRM
scanout. SDL's KMSDRM_GLES_SwapWindow wraps the flip in the full
lock_front_buffer / drmModeAddFB / drmModePageFlip pipeline (that's
what actually promotes the GBM front buffer to the scanout plane).
Bare eglSwapBuffers just cycles the EGL back buffer.

Fix: on rk3568 (ADVDRASTIC_SDL_GL), GFX_Flip calls SDL_GL_SwapWindow
instead of eglSwapBuffers. Everything else same as v5.

Guarded by ADVDRASTIC_SDL_GL, defined only on rk3568. h700/a133 code
paths unchanged.

Signed-off-by: James Pharaoh <james@pharaoh.uk>
